[KiCad-IOS port] eda_doc.cpp: guard MIME-manager use on wxUSE_MIMETYPE

GetAssociatedDocument() resolves non-PDF documentation files through
wxMimeTypesManager. Under wxQt there is no wxMimeTypesManager backend
(wx's only implementation uses macOS LaunchServices/legacy UTI APIs,
absent on iOS), so this port builds wx with wxUSE_MIMETYPE=OFF and the
types do not exist. Guard the fallback table and the lookup block on
wxUSE_MIMETYPE; without it the function takes its existing failure
path ("Unknown MIME type for documentation file") — PDF documents,
the common case, are handled separately by OpenPDF() and unaffected.

Modified file (GPL-3.0-or-later, same license as upstream):
  common/eda_doc.cpp

--- a/common/eda_doc.cpp
+++ b/common/eda_doc.cpp
@@ -38,6 +38,7 @@
 
 
 //  Mime type extensions (PDF files are not considered here)
+#if wxUSE_MIMETYPE
 static wxMimeTypesManager*  mimeDatabase;
 static const wxFileTypeInfo EDAfallbacks[] =
 {
@@ -58,6 +59,7 @@
     // must terminate the table with this!
     wxFileTypeInfo()
 };
+#endif // wxUSE_MIMETYPE
 
 
 bool GetAssociatedDocument( wxWindow* aParent, const wxString& aDocName, PROJECT* aProject,
@@ -179,6 +181,7 @@
